[url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3838759919&l=english]English version[/url]

[h1]BridgeSpan 自由造桥[/h1]
在浅海和湖面上修桥，让陆军和商人从两岸通行。船只仍可经过桥下水域。

模组提供 1 格石桥，以及 2 格、3 格跨海大桥，均由城市生产；同一城市可以建多座。订阅后在“额外内容”中启用即可使用。

适用于 Windows 版《文明6》的《风云变幻》单人游戏。
[b]支持与[url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=2465378070]《和而不同（Harmony in Diversity）》[/url]搭配使用，石桥解锁会跟随其科技树调整。[/b]

[h2]桥梁与建造[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]石桥：[/b]跨度 1 格。原版科技树需要“工程”；和而不同科技树需要“拱券”。
[*][b]跨海大桥：[/b]跨度 2 或 3 格，研究“钢铁”后解锁。共用一个生产入口，按桥位显示跨度和费用。
[*]两类桥都需要先研究[b]造船术[/b]。
[/list]
[olist]
[*]订阅模组，等待下载完成，在“额外内容”中启用 BridgeSpan。
[*]研究造船术和相应桥梁科技。
[*]打开城市生产面板，选择石桥或跨海大桥，点击合法水格，确认桥位、费用和移除提示后开工。
[/olist]
一个水格有多个合法桥位时，可在“方案 1、方案 2……”中选择；移到选项上可预览桥身及 A、B 两岸。只有一个方案时直接确认。

普通地图上可以看到施工中的桥；不需要另装启动器或手动替换文件。

[b]1 格石桥 / One-tile stone bridge[/b]
[img]https://images.steamusercontent.com/ugc/13916159276438813590/17BB25FF7E216130C0363D521ABC01FC6C2BF47C/[/img]
[b]3 格跨海大桥 / Three-tile sea bridge[/b]
[img]https://images.steamusercontent.com/ugc/9695476579627699561/94BCCF1BB26112B33242378ED4F23153C7695F48/[/img]

[h2]通行规则[/h2]
陆军和商人从桥的两端上下桥，不能从桥身侧面进出。过桥后的移动和战斗仍按游戏规则结算；能否继续攻击取决于剩余移动力、地形和控制区等条件。其他文明的陆军也需要满足登船科技条件。

[b]船只可以穿过桥身水格 / Ships can cross the bridge's water tiles[/b]
[img]https://images.steamusercontent.com/ugc/9239203255754149353/F68AFA9FCDA5C7B7545E90F7223E58B5FF906054/[/img]

[h2]实战截图：斯德哥尔摩[/h2]
真实地球地图中，斯德哥尔摩右侧的石桥连接了两岸。下方是骑兵从东岸过桥，到达西岸桥头的前后两张图。

[b]过桥前 / Before crossing[/b]
[img]https://images.steamusercontent.com/ugc/11182126203332235522/8D2E48F8164EE7C09809F9F7099167A21B35C63A/[/img]
[b]过桥后 / After crossing[/b]
[img]https://images.steamusercontent.com/ugc/14418814549652152040/8B8EA38C5678589E5240CD875DE7207B7A096837/[/img]
[i]两图由同局第 81 回合存档补录，展示过桥移动。[/i]

[h2]选址条件[/h2]
[list]
[*]沿直线跨越 1—3 格连续浅海或湖面，两端必须是可用陆地。不支持深海或折线桥。
[*]所有桥身水格必须属于同一座生产城市；同一文明的不同城市也不能混用。
[*]桥身不能占用资源或其他区域。允许移除的地貌和改良设施会在开工前提示；取消不会清理，确认后随建造移除。移除地貌仍需满足对应科技条件，不会获得建造者收获收益。
[*]山脉、运河和阻挡桥头的悬崖等可能使岸端不可用。
[/list]

[h2]反馈[/h2]
建有桥梁的存档请保持本模组启用。反馈问题时，请附桥位截图和复现步骤；有问题发生前的存档更好。

[h2]源码与共同开发[/h2]
欢迎一起完善 BridgeSpan！可以在 GitHub 提交问题和功能建议，参与翻译、测试、Lua / UI 开发或桥梁模型美术，也欢迎通过 Pull Request 贡献代码。
[url=https://github.com/civs6-mods/BridgeSpan]GitHub 源码仓库与开发协作[/url]

[hr][/hr]
[url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3838759919&l=schinese]简体中文版[/url]

[h1]BridgeSpan — Build Your Own Bridges[/h1]
BridgeSpan adds bridges across coast and lake tiles. Land units and traders can cross between the shores, while ships can still pass through the bridge's water tiles.

Build a one-tile stone bridge or a two-/three-tile sea bridge through city production. A city can build more than one bridge. Subscribe, let Steam finish downloading, and enable BridgeSpan in Additional Content.

For the Windows edition of Civilization VI, using the Gathering Storm ruleset in single-player.
[b]Compatible with [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=2465378070]Harmony in Diversity[/url]. The stone bridge unlock follows its technology tree.[/b]

[h2]Bridges and construction[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Stone bridge:[/b] spans one water tile. Requires Engineering in the standard technology tree, or Arch with Harmony in Diversity.
[*][b]Sea bridge:[/b] spans two or three water tiles and unlocks at Steel. Both lengths share one production entry; the placement preview shows the span and production cost.
[*]Both types also require [b]Shipbuilding[/b].
[/list]
[olist]
[*]Subscribe, wait for the download to finish, and enable BridgeSpan in Additional Content.
[*]Research Shipbuilding and the required bridge technology.
[*]Choose a bridge in the city production panel, select a valid water tile, then check the placement, cost and any removal warnings before confirming.
[/olist]
When a tile offers several valid layouts, choose Option 1, Option 2, and so on. Hover over an option to preview the bridge tiles and shores A and B. A single valid layout goes straight to confirmation.

Bridges have a construction model on the normal map. No separate launcher or manual file replacement is needed.

[b]One-tile stone bridge[/b]
[img]https://images.steamusercontent.com/ugc/13916159276438813590/17BB25FF7E216130C0363D521ABC01FC6C2BF47C/[/img]
[b]Three-tile sea bridge[/b]
[img]https://images.steamusercontent.com/ugc/9695476579627699561/94BCCF1BB26112B33242378ED4F23153C7695F48/[/img]

[h2]Movement[/h2]
Land units and traders enter and leave at the two ends, not along the sides. Normal movement and combat rules still apply: attacking after crossing depends on remaining movement, terrain, zones of control and other game rules. Land units from other civilizations also need the required embarkation technology. Ships can cross the water tiles occupied by the bridge.

[b]Ships can cross the bridge's water tiles[/b]
[img]https://images.steamusercontent.com/ugc/9239203255754149353/F68AFA9FCDA5C7B7545E90F7223E58B5FF906054/[/img]

[h2]In-game example: Stockholm[/h2]
The stone bridge east of Stockholm connects the shores on a real-world map. These screenshots show cavalry before crossing from the east bank and after reaching the west bridgehead. Both were captured by replaying turn 81 of the same save.

[b]Before crossing[/b]
[img]https://images.steamusercontent.com/ugc/11182126203332235522/8D2E48F8164EE7C09809F9F7099167A21B35C63A/[/img]
[b]After crossing[/b]
[img]https://images.steamusercontent.com/ugc/14418814549652152040/8B8EA38C5678589E5240CD875DE7207B7A096837/[/img]

[h2]Placement[/h2]
[list]
[*]A straight crossing of one to three consecutive coast or lake tiles, with usable land at both ends. Deep ocean and bent bridges are not supported.
[*]Every bridge water tile must belong to the same city that builds it. Tiles from another city cannot be included, even under the same civilization.
[*]Bridge tiles cannot contain resources or other districts. Removable features and improvements are listed before construction. Cancelling leaves them intact; confirming allows their removal during construction. Feature removal still requires the relevant technology and grants no builder harvest yields.
[*]Mountains, canals or cliffs blocking a bridgehead can make the shore unsuitable.
[/list]

[h2]Feedback[/h2]
Keep BridgeSpan enabled in saves containing its bridges. For bug reports, include a bridge screenshot and reproduction steps. A save from before the issue is especially useful.

[h2]Source & Contributions[/h2]
Help improve BridgeSpan! Report bugs, suggest features, contribute translations or testing, work on Lua / UI or bridge models and art, or submit a pull request on GitHub.
[url=https://github.com/civs6-mods/BridgeSpan]GitHub source code & contributions[/url]
